{"term":"工口","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"gōngkǒu","category":"internet_subculture","subcategory":"erotic content label","concept":"erotica","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":30,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":62,"recognition_pct_peak":72,"peak_year":2013,"regional":null,"definition":"A visual cipher representing the Japanese word エロ (ero, meaning erotic); the characters 工 and 口 together approximate the katakana エ and ロ in appearance, used as a censorship-evading label for erotic content.","english_term":"erotic content","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Originated in Japanese internet culture as a text-filter workaround. Somewhat archaic among younger Chinese users who prefer newer evasion terms. Understood primarily within ACG (anime, comics, games) communities."}
{"term":"H","lang":"zh","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"internet_subculture","subcategory":"lewdness label","concept":"lewdness","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"loanword","crude":20,"technical":0,"recognition_pct_current":68,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Borrowed from Japanese エッチ (ecchi, the letter H); an adjective or noun labeling sexually lewd or suggestive content, milder than explicit pornography.","english_term":"lewd","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"In Japanese, H is a euphemistic reading derived from 変態 (hentai) via its romaji initial. Adopted into Chinese ACG internet culture. Slightly archaic among Gen Z Chinese users who tend to prefer 涩 or 色."}
{"term":"涩图","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"sè tú","category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"pornographic images","concept":"nude_images","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":45,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexually explicit or pornographic images; uses 涩 (astringent) as a near-homophone substitute for 色 (lustful/sexual) to evade automated content moderation.","english_term":"porn images","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The character swap (涩 for 色) is a standard Chinese internet censorship-evasion technique called 谐音梗 (homophonic substitution). 涩 has no inherent sexual meaning; the evasion is transparent to human readers while defeating keyword filters."}
{"term":"色图","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"sè tú","category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"pornographic images","concept":"nude_images","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":55,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexually explicit or pornographic images; 色 here directly means lustful or sexual.","english_term":"porn images","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The direct form of 涩图; 色 carries unambiguous sexual meaning in this compound. Both 色图 and 涩图 are functionally synonymous, but 涩图 is preferred on platforms with keyword filtering."}
{"term":"本子","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"běnzi","category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"erotic fan comics","concept":"doujinshi","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":20,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":75,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'booklet' or 'notebook'; slang for doujinshi—self-published fan comics, often sexually explicit, typically based on characters from existing anime, manga, or games.","english_term":"doujinshi","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"The term is completely euphemistic—本子 alone simply means any small booklet. Sexual meaning is entirely context-dependent. Borrowed from the Japanese doujinshi scene via Chinese ACG fandom."}
{"term":"无码","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"wú mǎ","category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"uncensored pornography","concept":"pornography","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":55,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'without mosaic'; pornographic content, especially Japanese AV, that lacks the legally required pixelation censoring genitalia.","english_term":"uncensored porn","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Paired antonym of 有码. Japanese law (Penal Code Article 175) requires genital mosaic in domestically distributed adult video; uncensored versions are technically illegal to produce in Japan but widely distributed abroad and online."}
