{"term":"擦边球","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"cā biān qiú","category":"internet_subculture","subcategory":"borderline sexual content","concept":"bawdy_humor","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":10,"technical":0,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":83,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'edge ball' (a table tennis shot grazing the table edge); content that is sexually suggestive or provocative while technically remaining within platform or legal content rules.","english_term":"borderline content","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The table tennis metaphor captures deliberate exploitation of content-moderation grey zones. Describes a strategy as much as a content type. No clean English concept equivalent; bawdy_humor is the nearest registry entry but misses the regulatory-gaming dimension."}
{"term":"性转","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"xìng zhuǎn","category":"internet_subculture","subcategory":"fictional gender transformation","concept":"cross_dressing","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":20,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":68,"recognition_pct_peak":73,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'sex/gender transformation'; primarily refers to fan fiction and art in which a character changes biological sex or gender; secondarily used informally for transgender or gender-nonconforming identity.","english_term":"gender swap","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Primary context is anime/manga fandom (equivalent to English 'genderbend' or Rule 63). cross_dressing is the nearest registry concept but 性转 specifically implies biological sex transformation, not only clothing change. Also used colloquially in transgender discourse in mainland China."}
{"term":"纸片人","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"zhǐpiàn rén","category":"internet_subculture","subcategory":"2D fictional character attachment object","concept":"fictional_2d_character","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"subculture","crude":5,"technical":0,"recognition_pct_current":63,"recognition_pct_peak":68,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'paper person'; a 2D animated or illustrated fictional character from anime, manga, or games who is the object of romantic or sexual attachment, contrasted with a real ('3D') person.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"none","notes":"Tone ranges from self-deprecating to affectionate. The term names the character as the object of desire, distinct from naming the person who is attracted. Analogous to Japanese 二次元 (2D world) culture and the 'waifu' phenomenon but more neutral and broader in scope."}
{"term":"老色批","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"lǎo sè pī","category":"insults","subcategory":"lecherous veteran","concept":"lecherous_old_man","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":70,"technical":0,"recognition_pct_current":73,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'veteran/old sex maniac'; a pejorative, or affectionately self-applied, term for an older male who is obsessively and publicly focused on sex.","english_term":"dirty old man","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"老 (old/veteran) intensifies the base 色批. Used as genuine insult or ironic self-label in online male communities. The 'veteran' reading of 老 implies experienced, which softens it slightly compared to pure condemnation."}
{"term":"色批","lang":"zh","script":"hans","romanization":"sè pī","category":"insults","subcategory":"lecher","concept":"lecher","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":65,"technical":0,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":83,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A person, typically male, who is obsessively and inappropriately fixated on sex; a pervert or lecher; frequently self-applied with ironic humor in online communities.","english_term":"perv","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"批 functions as a crude collective-noun or intensifier suffix; 色 (lustful/sexual) is the root. Harsher than 好色 (fond of sex) but softer than a serious insult; widely embraced as a self-deprecating label in ACG and male internet subcultures."}
